INSERT INTO `p3_uniprot` VALUES (67,'development','human','9606','7124','P01375','Tumor necrosis factor',1,1,'exact_GeneID_cross_reference','Cytokine that binds to TNFRSF1A/TNFR1 and TNFRSF1B/TNFBR, activating the tumor necrosis factor-mediated (TNF) signaling pathway (PubMed:16284179, PubMed:33495445, PubMed:3883195, PubMed:6392892, PubMed:9435233). The TNF signaling pathway acts as a master regulator of the immune system, which either (1) promotes cell survival and inflammation by activating the canonical NF-kappa-B pathway or (2) trigger programmed cell death (apoptosis and necroptosis) (PubMed:16284179). Impairs regulatory T-cells (Treg) function in individuals with rheumatoid arthritis via FOXP3 dephosphorylation: acts by up-regulating the expression of protein phosphatase 1 (PP1), which dephosphorylates the key \'Ser-418\' residue of FOXP3, thereby inactivating FOXP3 and rendering Treg cells functionally defective (PubMed:23396208). Key mediator of cell death in the anticancer action of BCG-stimulated neutrophils in combination with DIABLO/SMAC mimetic in the RT4v6 bladder cancer cell line (PubMed:16829952, PubMed:22517918, PubMed:23396208). Induces insulin resistance in adipocytes via inhibition of insulin-induced IRS1 tyrosine phosphorylation and insulin-induced glucose uptake (By similarity). Induces GKAP42 protein degradation in adipocytes which is partially responsible for TNF-induced insulin resistance (By similarity). Plays a role in angiogenesis by inducing VEGF production synergistically with IL1B and IL6 (PubMed:12794819). Promotes osteoclastogenesis and therefore mediates bone resorption (By similarity) Cytokine mainly secreted by macrophages that binds to TNFRSF1A/TNFR1 and TNFRSF1B/TNFBR, activating the tumor necrosis factor-mediated (TNF) signaling pathway (PubMed:11592999, PubMed:16284179, PubMed:33495445, PubMed:3883195, PubMed:6392892). The TNF signaling pathway acts as a master regulator of the immune system, which either (1) promotes cell survival and inflammation by activating the canonical NF-kappa-B pathway or (2) trigger programmed cell death (apoptosis and necroptosis) (PubMed:16284179) The TNF intracellular domain (ICD) form induces IL12 production in dendritic cells The TNF intracellular domain (ICD) form induces IL12 production in dendritic cells','[\"GO:0000976\",\"GO:0002020\",\"GO:0005125\",\"GO:0005164\",\"GO:0042802\",\"GO:0140072\"]','[\"GO:0000122\",\"GO:0001666\",\"GO:0001774\",\"GO:0001819\",\"GO:0001937\",\"GO:0001975\",\"GO:0002037\",\"GO:0002281\",\"GO:0002439\",\"GO:0002639\",\"GO:0002719\",\"GO:0003009\",\"GO:0003085\",\"GO:0006954\",\"GO:0006955\",\"GO:0007259\",\"GO:0007623\",\"GO:0008625\",\"GO:0009410\",\"GO:0009615\",\"GO:0009651\",\"GO:0009750\",\"GO:0010459\",\"GO:0010573\",\"GO:0010628\",\"GO:0010629\",\"GO:0010744\",\"GO:0010888\",\"GO:0014823\",\"GO:0019722\",\"GO:0031334\",\"GO:0031622\",\"GO:0031642\",\"GO:0031663\",\"GO:0031667\",\"GO:0032715\",\"GO:0032722\",\"GO:0032724\",\"GO:0032731\",\"GO:0032741\",\"GO:0032755\",\"GO:0032757\",\"GO:0033209\",\"GO:0034116\",\"GO:0034138\",\"GO:0035900\",\"GO:0036005\",\"GO:0042311\",\"GO:0043065\",\"GO:0043068\",\"GO:0043122\",\"GO:0043123\",\"GO:0043243\",\"GO:0043410\",\"GO:0043525\",\"GO:0043537\",\"GO:0045071\",\"GO:0045429\",\"GO:0045471\",\"GO:0045598\",\"GO:0045599\",\"GO:0045668\",\"GO:0045672\",\"GO:0045732\",\"GO:0045760\",\"GO:0045785\",\"GO:0045840\",\"GO:0045892\",\"GO:0045893\",\"GO:0045930\",\"GO:0045944\",\"GO:0046325\",\"GO:0046330\",\"GO:0046677\",\"GO:0048143\",\"GO:0048566\",\"GO:0048661\",\"GO:0050729\",\"GO:0050768\",\"GO:0050796\",\"GO:0050806\",\"GO:0050807\",\"GO:0050890\",\"GO:0050901\",\"GO:0050966\",\"GO:0050995\",\"GO:0051044\",\"GO:0051222\",\"GO:0051384\",\"GO:0051798\",\"GO:0051897\",\"GO:0051966\",\"GO:0060252\",\"GO:0060557\",\"GO:0061044\",\"GO:0061048\",\"GO:0070374\",\"GO:0070886\",\"GO:0071300\",\"GO:0071316\",\"GO:0071346\",\"GO:0071479\",\"GO:0071677\",\"GO:0071803\",\"GO:0072577\",\"GO:007